## Why This Is Asked
Real-world enterprise risk monitoring requires multilingual understanding with code-switching while preserving privacy. It also tests ability to design federated updates, per-tenant governance, and secure rollback in production.

## Key Concepts
- Federated learning and differential privacy for cross-tenant training
- Multilingual handling with code-switching and low-resource languages
- Real-time alerting vs. post-hoc review pipeline
- Explainability and per-message risk scoring
- Drift detection and secure rollout/rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
function riskScore(tokens, model) {
  // placeholder: real inference would run a lightweight classifier
  // returns 0..1 risk probability for the message
  const score = model.predict(tokens);
  return Math.max(0, Math.min(1, score));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate drift across tenants and under new vocabularies?
- What security controls ensure privacy while enabling per-tenant explainability?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a real-time, privacy-preserving credibility-verification pipeline with multilingual support and explainability, plus practical KVs like drift handling and rollback.

## Key Concepts

- Retrieval-augmented NLP and multilingual inference
- On-device preprocessing and privacy-preserving cloud inference
- Real-time latency budgeting (<250 ms)
- Explainability with citations
- Drift detection, model/versioning, rollback strategy

## Code Example

```javascript
function processMessage(msg) {
  const clean = preprocess(msg);
  const vec = encodeQuery(clean);
  const evidence = retrieveKB(vec);
  const score = scoreCredibility(evidence, msg);
  return explain(evidence, score);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you calibrate the credibility detector to minimize false positives in customer-support contexts?
- How would you design the rollback plan if the KB evidence becomes stale or compromised?
